+/* A title's `current` reaching its ring's end is not yet an overrun (cellGcmSys.c).
+ *
+ * The title fills the ring, then calls its callback, and for that instant `current`
+ * reads end. A drain landing there used to recycle the ring on the title's behalf,
+ * dropping every queued command, flip included, and PES 2013 then waited for that flip
+ * forever. A title that really is stuck at end, as AMGL's callback leaves it, must still
+ * be recycled, and an end position that keeps moving is not stuck.
+ *
+ * clang -std=gnu17 -w -I include -I libs/video -I runtime/platform -Wl,-dead_strip
+ *   -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections -pthread libs/video/tests/test_gcm_overrun.c
+ *   runtime/platform/win32_compat.c -o /tmp/test_gcm_overrun
+ */
